## Delivery

`SKILL.md` keeps examples inline. `SKILL.compact.md` is the rules-only, example-free extract; do not routinely fetch examples when using it. Delivery format is independent of behaviour mode.

Keep settings within available session context. Cross-session persistence, command registration, and always-on injection require host support. Applying this skill must not change host prompts, hooks, or settings.

## Final check

Before returning work: request met or blocker named; scope preserved; validation truthful; meaning intact; requested format followed.

USER'S CURRENT SCOPE: Six creature families, three morphology variants each. Existing base morphology is shared by Sunlight + Twilight. One distinct, more intimidating Midnight + Abyss form per family. One advanced Trench form per family. Three forms are therefore: Base → Midnight/Abyss → Trench. Preserve the existing six creature base originals unchanged. The base's primary/secondary/tertiary regions receive a richer offline palette profile (three stepped shades per role) so it no longer uses the weak single hot pink/cyan/lime swatches. This offline recolour changes no anatomy and is still replaceable by the three role masks. Generate only the 12 new morphology forms (six Midnight/Abyss + six Trench); do not re-generate the six base morphologies.

Scope counts: 6 families × 3 variant profiles = 18 final morphology/profile assets; 6 use existing native bases, 12 are new native Codex PNGs. Sunlight and Twilight link to the same Base asset; Midnight and Abyss link to the same single midpoint asset; Trench links to its separate advanced form. Keep this mapping exact in the report and viewer. The separate original six-style × five-depth transparent composition work under ocean-style-prototypes/creature-assets remains unchanged and should be separately evidenced; do not replace it with these individual family variants.

COLORABILITY: keep three semantic regions: primary, secondary and tertiary. Apply three related profile tones (shadow/base/highlight) to each region, per `palette-profiles.json`, plus neutral outline/detail colors. Nine species-specific role-shades total + three neutrals. Do not use the old garish one-color-per-region magenta/cyan/lime profile. Parent's offline exporter maps the native output to the precise role palette after reviewing the actual imagery. Shade clusters should follow the body/lighting, not random speckles; role groups remain distinct and anatomically contiguous. This allows future palette swap by role or shade.

PROVIDER: Codex built-in image_gen.imagegen, existing logged-in ChatGPT account only. Exactly 12 new native image-generation outputs: for each six families, one Midnight/Abyss image and one Trench image. No new base generation. No RetroDiffusion, other providers, external API, purchases/subscriptions, credit purchase, fallback or paid rerolls. User explicitly requested deeper creature variants. Native quota/price is unknown; report truthfully. Stop if native generation is unavailable. One call per target, no retries or extras.

WRITE ONLY in C:/SyncedProjects/Websites/Vultr-Phishing-Sandbox/ocean-style-prototypes/codex-creature-depth-evolution plus normal Codex image staging. `inputs/`, `palette-profiles.json` and the six prior base originals elsewhere are read-only. Save returned native RGBA files unchanged to `<family>-midnight-abyss-native.png` or `<family>-trench-native.png`. Save/append generation-report.json immediately for each success with exact prompt, family/stage, target depths, tool, references/hashes, native staging path/hash, copied source hash, dimensions/alpha/request count, and any recovery errors. Verify existing output targets before skipping; never overwrite. Preserve all prior neon base files and prior Codex color-coded studies.

Both references for each family are mapped in `reference-manifest.json`:
- `*-anatomy-reference.png`: actual selected family sprite; preserve its distinctive body plan, orientation and defining features.
- `*-role-map-reference.png`: the earlier vivid segmented sprite, showing primary/secondary/tertiary BODY REGION PLACEMENT ONLY. Ignore its three placeholder colors; use species-specific nine-shade palette in `palette-profiles.json`.

COMMON STYLE: consistent crisp SNES/PC98 style of game sprite, square transparent canvas, full creature centered with generous empty margin, same family view scale, visible dark stepped outline, flat/stepped 2–3 tones per role, no 3D, soft paint, gradients, checkerboards, background, text, labels, frames or detached props. All important parts fit within margins. Native outputs retain true alpha. Use a single complete creature, not a spritesheet.

MIDNIGHT/ABYSS: one moderately evolved, more fearsome version. Keep the same family and recognizable skeleton/silhouette. Modestly strengthen appropriate traits: fangs/jaw/armor/lure/photophores, not new heads or random limb additions. Colors follow its role profile and stay vivid/readable; final level darkness is applied by palette mapping.

TRENCH: one distinctly more advanced form per family, still connected to its family: anglerfish with broader giant jaw/extended lure; viperfish with large deep predator body and longer needle fangs, not generic shark; siphonophore as larger but still single connected colony; host fish as an armored giant while its parasite remains attached inside the mouth; cookiecutter as megalodon-inspired giant shark while preserving a dark collar or circular bite motif; octopus as enormous kraken with exactly eight distinct connected arms. No gore, extra organisms, severed parts, unrelated species or visible fear/strength stats. Keep all three replaceable color-role regions in both new forms.

